# The source file of this conversion, pinned.
#
# convert_ism.py reads it from sources/ism.json (git-ignored). The Validators
# workflow downloads it from the base below, checks it against this list
# with `sha256sum -c`, runs the converter and fails if the conversion in this
# folder comes out different. The bundle and the two coverage reports are
# therefore a reproducible record: a change of the kernel, of
# oscal_conv_lib.py or of the converter that would alter them is noticed.
#
# The base is the publisher's mirror at the tag of release 2026.06.18. The
# file is saved under the name the converter reads.
#
# base: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AustralianCyberSecurityCentre/ism-oscal/v2026.06.18/
# into: sources
# path: ISM_catalog.json -> ism.json
#
